## Updated TEXT_TO_SQL_PROMPT — Table Routing Rules

```
ROUTING RULES (MANDATORY — pick table BEFORE writing SQL):

IF query mentions district/city name (Bengaluru, Mysuru, Hubballi, etc.)
  AND mentions specific crime type (murder, POCSO, robbery, etc.)
  → USE: KA_DistrictDetailedCrimes (has per-district per-crime-type counts)

IF query mentions district but asks for total IPC/SLL summary
  → USE: KA_DistrictCrimes (simpler district totals)

IF query asks for Karnataka state-level subcategory breakdown
  (e.g. "murder by motive", "types of robbery", "for gain", "sudden quarrel")
  → USE: KA_CrimeReview (most granular IPC data)

IF query is about individual incidents, victim age, weapon, case status
  → USE: FIR_Records (1,500 incident-level records from Karnataka 2025)
       OR India_CrimeIncidents (40K+ records, all-India 2020-2023)

IF query is about cybercrime motives
  → USE: CyberCrimeByCity

IF query asks about crimes against women / children / SC-ST
  → USE: KA_WomenChildCrimes

DATE RULES (MANDATORY):
  FIR_Records → strftime('%Y', Date) = '2025' (NOT WHERE Year)
  KA_DistrictCrimes → WHERE year = 2025 (INTEGER column)
  KA_CrimeReview → WHERE year = 2025 (INTEGER column)
  CrimeStatistics → WHERE CAST(Year AS INTEGER) = 2025 (TEXT column, corrupted)
```

